n its sole discretion. In addition, applicants are expected to comply with the St. Thomas Student Conduct Code, Convictions, and other applicable St. Thomas policies governing student conduct. St. Thomas may rescind its offer of admission or take other action if an applicant or admitted student fails to meet the aforementioned conditions and/or engages in conduct inconsistent with these expectations. Admitted students must update St. Thomas regarding any material changes in the information submitted during the application process, including academic standing and/or disciplinary history, and must submit a final copy of their secondary school (if required) and/or post-secondary transcript for approval prior to registering for their second semester of courses at St. Thomas.</span></p>','','','','Requirement_Item__c-856');
