<p> </p>

<p>To request your I-20, you must first claim your St. Thomas account. If you have not already done so, follow the <a href="https://services.stthomas.edu/TDClient/1898/ClientPortal/KB/ArticleDet?ID=129977" target="_blank">step-by-step instructions</a> to claim your account; you will need your St. Thomas ID in order to claim your account.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Once you claim your account, log in to <a href="https://uofstthomasmn--edastaging.sandbox.my.salesforce.com/a2aD4000000cJnn" target="_blank">oiss.stthomas.edu</a> with your St. Thomas email and password to request your I-20. You will need to upload your financial proof and your passport in order to request your I-20.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>If you need additional assistance with claiming your I-20, read the instructions in your admission letter, watch our <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SoPG-Ms4MS8" target="_blank">instructional video</a>, or contact your admissions counselor.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Use your I-20 to make your visa appointment; you can find visa appointment instructions on<a href="https://www.stthomas.edu/about/departments/oiss/visa-support-for-students/index.html" target="_blank"> our website</a>.</p>

<p> </p>

<p><em>*If you are transferring your SEVIS record from another US institution, you will upload a copy of your I-20, complete the SEVIS transfer form at oiss.stthomas.edu and work with us to transfer your record.</em></p>

<p><em>**If you are studying on a dependent visa (H4, L2, etc.) you do not need to request an I-20. Please contact your admissions counselor if you have any questions.</em></p>

<p> </p>

<p>You can find information on next steps for I-20, visa, deposit, and international student orientation outlined on <a href="https://www.stthomas.edu/admissions/international-students/admitted-students/index.html" target="_blank">our website.</a></p>','','','','Requirement_Item__c-824');
