Along with receiving support from your principal (teachers) or your pastor (parish educators) and verification of employment from the Archdiocese, applicants must write an essay that responds to the three points below.
<br>
<br>
<ul>

<li>Summarize your educational experience (degrees, certificates, licenses, etc.). Note the St. Thomas program you are applying to and address how this program relates to your professional goals as well as the needs/goals of the school or parish in which you are currently working. </li>

<li>Reflect on your sense of vocation as an educator in a Catholic school/parish. </li>

<li>Finally, affirm that by accepting Murray funding, you are making a commitment to work in the Archdiocese for at least three years upon completion of your program. </li>
</ol>
<br>
<i>A complete essay responds to all three points. Your total word count should be between 500 and 750 words. Please submit your essay in a Word document (.doc or .docx) or PDF document (.pdf).  </i>

<br>

