Merit-based scholarships are available to select candidates with strong applications. All applicants are automatically considered for the Dean’s Scholarship. No separate essay is required. This award may not be stacked with other scholarships or discounts.

<br>
<br>
<center><Font size=4 Font color=#6d3696><b>Tommie Alumni Scholarship</b></Font></center>

<br>

All St. Thomas undergraduate alumni are automatically awarded the Tommie Alumni Scholarship to cover tuition for one 3-credit course. No separate essay is required. This award may not be stacked with other scholarships or discounts.
<br>
<br>

<center><Font size=4 Font color=#6d3696><b>Diversity and Inclusion Scholarship</b></Font></center>

<br>

Scholarships are available to applicants who demonstrate a history of academic and professional success, leadership, service, and engagement in cultural or cross-cultural initiatives in previous academic, professional, or volunteer settings. Strong candidates will be domestic candidates with two or more years of full-time work experience after college graduation, have a strong undergraduate academic record, and show evidence of committed involvement in activities, programs, or initiatives that foster inclusion, cross-cultural awareness, or a commitment to diversity in its many forms. <b>To be considered, review the scholarship requirements on our website and submit a statement </b>(no more than 300 words) describing the most relevant experiences that qualify you for this award. This award may not be stacked with other scholarships or discounts.
<br>
<br>

<center><Font size=4 Font color=#6d3696><b>Non-Profit Scholarship: Business for the Common Good</b></Font></center>

<br>

Applicants who work in the non-profit industry are encouraged to apply for the Business for the Common Good scholarship. This scholarship awards up to $10,000 as long as you maintain good standing during the program.


<br>
<br>

In order to qualify, applicants must meet the following criteria:

<ul class="indented">
<li>Currently work full-time for an organization with 501(c)(3) tax-exempt non-profit status</li>
<li>Currently work full-time for a small or medium-sized non-profit organization OR work for an organization that is a member of the Minnesota Council of Nonprofits</li>
</ul>

<br>

Increased consideration will be given to applicants who work at organizations that:

<ul class="indented">
<li>Generate fewer than $90,000 per year in revenue</li>
<li>Directly serve members of the community</li>
<li>Provide services in high need areas including homelessness, poverty, and access</li>
</ul>

<br>

To apply for this scholarship during the application process, please submit a statement in the applicant portal that identifies your organization and demonstrates your commitment to nonprofit work. This award may not be stacked with other scholarships or discounts.

<br>
<br>

<b>To apply to any of the scholarships list above, please submit ONE file below. </b>

<br>
<br>

